	<key>DESCRIPTION</key>
	<string>Modul8's side of dots's Modul8 mode on the modGrid iPad app. dots owns the iPad; in its Modul8 mode (the right column's lower button) it passes the 16 dials and the two rows of buttons above the grid here over the 'dots modGrid' port (pick it in the list if it isn't picked; dots's library MIDI tab can use an IAC bus instead). The layout is the Twister module's Modul8 side: dials 1, 5, 9, 13 are four layers' alpha and buttons 1, 5, 9, 13 select them (button 16 moves them to layers 6-9); dials 2-4 the colour (buttons 2-4 switch each between modulate and additive); dials 6-8 saturation, lightness and contrast with buttons 6-8 turning them on; dials 10-12 scale, speed and transition; dial 16 the crossfader; buttons 14 and 15 master invert and flash. Values and colours go back to the iPad through dots; the names on the iPad come from dots (bin/data/modul8.json replaces the built-in ones when this layout changes).</string>
	<key>MODULE_AUTOFLUSH</key>
	<false/>
	<key>MODULE_CONTROL_ID_COUNTER</key>
